      "id": 1,
      "text": "The town was officially established on March 31, 1864, and renamed after Colonel James Madison Wesson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wesson%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1866, Wesson founded the Mississippi Manufacturing Company, a textile mill that became a local economic hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wesson%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The mills were destroyed by fire in 1873, and four new mill buildings were built between 1873 and 1894.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wesson%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wesson's first public school was built in 1875, and Copiah-Lincoln Junior College opened in 1928.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wesson%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Route 51 passes through Wesson, leading north 11 miles to Hazlehurst and south 9 miles to Brookhaven.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
